n-expected Democratic wave in Harris County, would move this toward tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": []}, "overview": "Texas's 9th District is a new Republican-leaning Houston-area seat drawn after redistricting, and an open-seat contest there favors Republican Alex Mealer. Mealer, endorsed by Trump, won a contentious primary runoff over state Rep. Briscoe Cain and has built a commanding financial lead: about $2.1 million raised with nearly $4.8 million in outside support, against roughly $55,000 for Democrat Leticia Gutierrez, who has drawn no outside spending.\n\nTwo recent polls of likely voters put Mealer ahead 48 to 42, and nearly all race raters call the seat Likely Republican, with markets giving Gutierrez about a one-in-six chance. A Democratic-tilted national environment and news that Mealer's campaign has scrubbed Trump from its website suggest some vulnerability, but the district's fundamentals still point clearly toward Mealer.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0912, "margin": -8.44}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0891, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0766, "margin": -10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1178, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0737, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0642, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0775, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0899, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0901, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0919, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1301, "margin": -7.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1157, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.1517, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0916, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0727, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0914, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0573, "margin": -9.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.0729